.\" Installed by cmake --install and by the Debian package. The version is the
.\" same frozen Git identity compiled into the daemon.
.TH CORELETD 8 "August 2026" "coreletd @CORELETD_VERSION@" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
coreletd \- MeshCore daemon for the ClockworkPi uConsole with AIO v2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coreletd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B coreletd
drives the SX1262 LoRa transceiver on the HackerGadgets / OpenSourceSDRLab
AIO v2 expansion board over
.BR spidev (4)
and libgpiod, speaks the MeshCore mesh protocol, and exposes the MeshCore
companion protocol over TCP so that the phone or web app,
.BR meshcore-cli (1)
and meshtui can connect \(em including from the uConsole itself over loopback.
.PP
It sends and receives adverts, maintains a contact store, carries encrypted
direct messages with acknowledgements, retries and path learning, and relays
channel (group) messages. Repeater and room server roles are not implemented,
and TCP is the only companion transport.
.PP
Everything runs on a single thread in one
.BR poll (2)
loop.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Read configuration from \fIPATH\fR instead of
.IR /etc/coreletd/coreletd.ini .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Raise the log level to debug, overriding the configuration file. Repeat for
trace, which reports every SPI command and IRQ.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-syslog
Omit timestamps from log lines, for running under systemd, which adds its own.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are grouped into
.BR [radio] ,
.BR [hardware] ,
.BR [node] ,
.BR [companion] ,
.BR [storage]
and
.B [logging]
sections.
.PP
.B lora_freq
in
.B [radio]
is required and has no default: which band you may transmit on is a legal
question, not a technical one. The daemon refuses to start without it. Every
node on a mesh must agree on
.BR lora_bw ,
.B lora_sf
and
.BR lora_cr .
The installed configuration file documents every option.
.PP
The AIO v2 gates power to each subsystem behind a GPIO. GPIO16 must be driven
high or the SX1262 is unpowered and every SPI read returns zeroes. The daemon
does not switch that rail: turn it on with whatever manages the board's power.
.PP
A radio that does not answer is therefore not a startup failure. The daemon
starts without one, retries every
.B lora_retry_interval
seconds from
.B [hardware]
(10 by default, 0 to disable), and picks the radio up as soon as it appears.
The same check notices a rail switched off while running: transmits are held
and the radio is brought back when power returns.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/coreletd/coreletd.ini
Configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/coreletd/identity
The node's Ed25519 signing key, generated on first start, mode 0600. This file
.I is
the node: back it up. Deleting it yields a new public key, and every contact
will see the node as a stranger.
.TP
.I /var/lib/coreletd/contacts
.TQ
.I /var/lib/coreletd/channels
Learned contacts and configured channels.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99\-coreletd.rules
Grants the
.B coreletd
group access to the SPI bus and the GPIO character devices, so the daemon need
not run as root.
.SH SECURITY
The companion protocol has no authentication whatsoever. Anyone who can reach
the port can read messages and send as this node, so
.B companion_bind
in
.B [companion]
defaults to 127.0.0.1. Widen it only on a trusted network, ideally behind an
SSH tunnel or WireGuard.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on a clean shutdown after SIGINT or SIGTERM, 1 if the configuration
cannot be loaded or the radio cannot be brought up, and 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR spidev (4)
.PP
/usr/share/doc/coreletd/README.Debian for uConsole setup, including the
device tree overlay the radio needs.
.SH AUTHOR
Denis Yantarev <denis.yantarev@gmail.com>
